# CH02 — Orders in Ashes. Veyr and the Underways. SC03 is the authored key scene.

@scene VEYR_WANTED
say narr | Veyr's south gate is doubled with guards. Dain's description is nailed to the post beside Tessa's.
say tessa | They spelled my name right this time. Progress.
@end

@scene T02_HERALD
say "Herald" | Hear it! Crown Quarry reopened by ministry inspection! Production restored! Heartglass to every lamp by winter!
say dain | That is not what happened.
say "Herald" | It's what's written, sir. I only read it.
@end

@scene T02_GUARDS
say guard | My family can't eat loyalty. That's all I'm saying.
say "Soldier" | Then say it quieter. Loyalty's what we're paid in this month.
say guard | Paid? We're paid in lamp oil and promises.
@end

@scene T02_VENDOR1
say keeper | Celebration prices! Everything's dearer because we're all very happy.
@end

@scene T02_VENDOR2
say baker | Crown loaves, stamped with the oath. Same bread as last week. Twice the price.
@end

@scene T02_LAMPMAN
say worker | Public heartglass lamps. Lovely warm light. Buzzes at night like a trapped wasp.
say worker | I'm told that's pressure.
@end

@scene T02_CHILD
say child | Are you the knight who stopped the quarry? The herald says a knight reopened it.
say dain | The herald is wrong.
say child | Can you tell him? He's very loud.
@end

@scene T02_CLERK_M
say clerk | Records open to the public? No. Records are open to the ministry, which is the public, in a sense.
@end

@scene T02_PILGRIM
say "Pilgrim" | I walked from Nacre to see the Oath Statue. It's smaller than the songs.
rumor | A pilgrim came from Nacre, north across the salt: 'a sanctuary where water remembers.'
@end

@scene T02_SMITH
say keeper | Blades and plate. The good stock goes to the Marshal's men first.
shop SHOP_T02
@end

@scene T02_AIDE
say "Ministry Aide" | Captain Ashward! The Marshal's office has your commendation ready. Step up to the oath square.
@end

@scene T02_GUARD_S
say guard | Oath Square, Captain. Stand where the aide shows you.
@end

@scene T02_ANSEL_SQ
say ansel | Clerk Ansel, gate records. You're the quarry captain.
say ansel | I refused a death certificate last month. Man was sitting in front of me. Alive. They found another clerk.
@end

@scene T02_WIDOW
say elder | My husband went to the quarry in a ministry cart. The ledger says he retired. I'd like to know where.
@end

@scene T02_ARCHIVIST
say scholar | The lower hall survives everything. That's what lower halls are for.
@end

@scene CH02_ARREST once
music M011
face player up
say "Ministry Aide" | Captain Dain Ashward. For the successful reopening of Crown Quarry, the Marshal's office commends -
say dain | The quarry did not reopen. I refused the restart. Seven workers were trapped below the lift.
say "Ministry Aide" | The report says -
say dain | The report is wrong. Correct it.
say "Ministry Aide" | ...Guards.
shake 0.3
say tessa | And that's why you don't correct a ministry in its own square.
say narr | The commendation ceremony ends early. The guards are polite about it.
fade out 0.6
warp D02_R01 cell right
fade in 0.6
music M020
say narr | Veyr Underways. Intake Hall. The cell smells of lamp oil and old paper.
say tessa | Relay tampering, for me. For you: 'insubordination and interference with production.'
say tessa | We're a matched set.
objective | Find a way out of the Intake Hall.
@end

@scene D02_JAILER
say guard | Sister Oriel's coming down to certify the apprentice. Mental fitness. Formality.
@end

@scene D02_ORIEL once
say oriel | Tessa Vale. I am here to certify whether you are fit to stand trial.
say tessa | Am I?
say oriel | I have not examined you yet. I have examined this.
say oriel | Your charge sheet is dated two days before the inspection. They wrote the charge before you did anything.
say dain | They knew.
say oriel | They knew what they intended to call it. That is not quite the same thing, but it is close enough to frighten me.
say oriel | There is a service door behind the ledger stacks.
say dain | Then we go.
say oriel | We take the records first. If you only run, you are fugitives. If you carry the ledgers, you are witnesses.
say tessa | I like being a witness. Witnesses get to talk.
set d02_oriel
join C06
say narr | Oriel's Prayer heals, cleanses and reveals what enemies have committed to. She cannot see what they have not chosen.
objective oriel | Take the ledgers from the Ledger Stacks, then leave by the canal.
@end

@scene D02_SC03 once
say narr | The ledger stacks. Rows of transport orders, each signed and countersigned.
say tessa | This one was signed before we reached the quarry.
say dain | They knew it would happen.
say oriel | They knew what they intended to call it.
say tessa | And this older one?
say oriel | Mine.
say dain | You did not know what they meant.
say oriel | I knew I had not asked.
say oriel | Take the ledger. All of it.
key K_LEDGER
say narr | The ledger names a transport origin: heartglass routed via the Rootward sluices, north of Veyr.
journal | Transport orders route heartglass via the Rootward sluices, north of Veyr.
objective oriel | Leave the Underways by the canal. The ledger points to Rootward.
@end

@scene D02_BELL
sfx FX031
if flag:d02_bell back
set d02_bell
say narr | The signal bell rings. Down the junction, two guards look up, check their chalk marks, and walk toward the echo in the south corridor.
end
label back
unset d02_bell
say narr | The bell rings again. The guards grumble and trudge back to the north corridor.
@end

@scene D02_PATROL
say guard | Post orders, whoever you are. We hold here until the bell says otherwise.
@end

@scene D02_DROP once
say narr | The walkway ends at a ledge above the cistern floor. There's a ladder further east - but this is quicker.
choice | Drop down -> drop | Stay up -> stay
label drop
move player down down down down
set d02_dropped
label stay
@end

@scene D02_BAILIFF once
music silence
say narr | A brass machine unfolds in the seal chamber, stamping a warrant against its own chest.
say "Brass Bailiff" | UNAUTHORIZED READERS. PRESENT YOUR WARRANT.
say tessa | We're more of a 'no warrant' household.
say oriel | It names its next target before it restrains them. Watch the paper.
battle B02 noflee
set b02_done
music M020
say narr | The Bailiff's stamp arm locks. Its warrants flutter to the floor, every one of them blank.
say oriel | It was built to arrest. It had nothing to arrest us for.
xp 80
objective | Reach the canal exit east of the seal chamber.
@end

@scene D02_ANSEL
say ansel | The canal gate. I was checking the latch. It seems I forgot to check it.
say ansel | If anyone asks, I was doing inventory.
@end

@scene CH02_CANAL once
say ansel | Go. The boat's old but it floats. I'll say you overpowered me. Nobody will believe it, but they'll write it down.
say dain | Thank you.
say ansel | Don't. Just - make it worth the inventory.
say oriel | Where does the ledger send us?
say tessa | Rootward. North of the city, where the irrigation sluices are. Whatever they're moving, it goes through there.
fade out 0.6
chapter CH02
set wanted
say narr | The boat slides out under the walls. Behind them, Veyr's bells ring for a commendation nobody attended.
warp WORLD l_d03 down
fade in 0.6
objective oriel | Follow the ledger to the Rootward sluices, just north.
discover L_D03
level_floor 6
@end
